 "glorious-assumption.about-this-story.text": ".",
 "glorious-assumption.about-this-story.the-gospel-passage-is-quoted-word-for-word-from-the-douay-rh": "The Gospel passage is quoted word for word from the Douay-Rheims Bible, 1899 American Edition, which is in the public domain; verse numbers are omitted for reading aloud, and … marks skipped verses. The Our Father, Hail Mary, Glory Be and Fatima prayers follow the standard formulas used across this site. This mystery is traditionally prayed on Wednesday / Sunday.",
 "glorious-assumption.about-this-story.the-church-teaches-that-mary-was-assumed-body-and-soul-into": "The Church teaches that Mary was assumed body and soul into heaven (Pope Pius XII, Munificentissimus Deus, 1950); the passage on the Gospel page is the traditional sign from the Book of Revelation.",
 "glorious-assumption.frequently-asked-questio.frequently-asked-questions": "Frequently Asked Questions",
 "glorious-assumption.frequently-asked-questio.what-is-the-fourth-glorious-mystery": "What is the Fourth Glorious Mystery?",
 "glorious-assumption.frequently-asked-questio.the-assumption-of-mary-when-mary-s-life-on-earth-was-finishe": "The Assumption of Mary. When Mary's life on earth was finished, God brought her, body and soul, into the glory of heaven. This mystery is traditionally prayed on Wednesday / Sunday, and its fruit is devotion to Mary and purity of heart.",
 "glorious-assumption.frequently-asked-questio.how-do-you-pray-this-decade-with-children": "How do you pray this decade with children?",
 "glorious-assumption.frequently-asked-questio.read-one-page-at-a-time-on-the-decade-page-pray-the-our-fath": "Read one page at a time. On the decade page, pray the Our Father once, the Hail Mary ten times (one for each bead), then the Glory Be and the Fatima prayer.",
